# A0 AArch64 emitter, written in A0. Fourth module of the self-hosted compiler (DESIGN.md 7a,
# stage 4a). Input: the checked word IR of compiler/check.a0 (pool sym fns nodes args tlist and
# the node types). Output: Darwin arm64 assembly text as bytes in a u32x4096 array plus its
# length, the module shape of src/arm64.ts: one `.globl _a0_<name>` block per function and the
# C-compatible calling convention for scalar signatures (parameter i in w0-w7, then the stack
# at Darwin's packing, u32 4 bytes and bool 1 byte; the result in w0), so the C test driver of
# tools/verify.ts links against it unchanged.
# Scope: functions whose parameters, result and every node are u32 or bool. Arrays, records
# and io are refused with diagnostic code 5 (fn node; node 4294967295 for a parameter or the
# result type); code 4 when a node's text exceeds the line buffer or the module the output.
# Scheme (first version, the shape of the first TypeScript backend; correctness over speed):
# every value lives in a stack slot and every call, fold and loop is a real `bl`. The frame:
#     x29 + 16 + ...        incoming stack parameters
#     x29                   saved x29, x30
#     sp + O + 4k           slot k: the parameters, then two slots per node (value, counter)
#     sp .. sp + O          outgoing stack arguments (O rounded to 16)
# A node loads its operands into w9-w11, computes into w12 and stores to its slot; a literal
# is movz/movk. The register allocator (a linear scan over w19-w28 as in src/arm64.ts), the
# inlining of small callees and in-place aggregates are stage 4b; they replace `lload`, the
# stores of `enodestep` and the `bl` of `argstep` without changing the text builders.
# Text: each node's lines are built in a line buffer (u32x512 bytes, length) by writers that
# take a flag and write nothing when it is false (how a node selects its instruction sequence
# without control flow), then appended once to the module buffer by `flush`. `lb` writes one
# byte, `lp` up to 16 bytes packed little-endian in four words (each constant is the ASCII of
# the string in its comment), `ldec` a decimal, `lname` a symbol's bytes. The writers are
# unrolled and the line buffer is small because the reference interpreter validates every
# array element of every call argument.
# This first version (`emitio`) is kept for tools/selfhost-verify.ts and tools/app.ts; the
# whole-language emitter the arm64 bootstrap uses (`qunit`, the q functions) follows it below.

use "emit_c.a0"

# up to 16 bytes packed little-endian in four words; zero bytes are skipped (unrolled)
fn lp (u32x512,u32) u32 u32 u32 u32 bool -> (u32x512,u32)
l0 at p0 0
n0 at p0 1
x0 shr p1 0
v0 and x0 255
z0 ne v0 0
o0 and p5 z0
c0 get l0 n0
u0 select o0 v0 c0
l1 set l0 n0 u0
a0 add n0 1
n1 select o0 a0 n0
x1 shr p1 8
v1 and x1 255
z1 ne v1 0
o1 and p5 z1
c1 get l1 n1
u1 select o1 v1 c1
l2 set l1 n1 u1
a1 add n1 1
n2 select o1 a1 n1
x2 shr p1 16
v2 and x2 255
z2 ne v2 0
o2 and p5 z2
c2 get l2 n2
u2 select o2 v2 c2
l3 set l2 n2 u2
a2 add n2 1
n3 select o2 a2 n2
x3 shr p1 24
v3 and x3 255
z3 ne v3 0
o3 and p5 z3
c3 get l3 n3
u3 select o3 v3 c3
l4 set l3 n3 u3
a3 add n3 1
n4 select o3 a3 n3
x4 shr p2 0
v4 and x4 255
z4 ne v4 0
o4 and p5 z4
c4 get l4 n4
u4 select o4 v4 c4
l5 set l4 n4 u4
a4 add n4 1
n5 select o4 a4 n4
x5 shr p2 8
v5 and x5 255
z5 ne v5 0
o5 and p5 z5
c5 get l5 n5
u5 select o5 v5 c5
l6 set l5 n5 u5
a5 add n5 1
n6 select o5 a5 n5
